WEBVTT

00:00:00.181 --> 00:00:02.508
Here's the ball from last time, launched at

00:00:02.608 --> 00:00:05.257
twenty-five metres per second, fifty degrees above the

00:00:05.297 --> 00:00:06.701
horizontal, from level ground.

00:00:07.303 --> 00:00:09.571
Its components are about sixteen point one across

00:00:10.013 --> 00:00:11.418
and nineteen point two up,

00:00:12.061 --> 00:00:13.044
and we followed it to the top.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:14.954
Now let's finish the flight.

00:00:15.558 --> 00:00:16.360
How high does it get,

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:17.886
and how long is it in the air?

00:00:18.572 --> 00:00:19.462
But first, a prediction.

00:00:20.131 --> 00:00:21.575
When it lands back at the level it

00:00:21.616 --> 00:00:24.224
started from, is it moving faster than at

00:00:24.265 --> 00:00:25.328
launch, slower,

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:26.773
or at the same speed?

00:00:27.481 --> 00:00:27.865
Have a think.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.094
Start with the height.

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:36.389
At the top, the vertical velocity is zero,

00:00:36.831 --> 00:00:38.196
and we don't need to know when that

00:00:38.258 --> 00:00:38.618
happens.

00:00:39.041 --> 00:00:41.307
So choose the equation without time in it,

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.377
v squared equals u squared plus two a

00:00:44.639 --> 00:00:46.203
s, written for the vertical column.

00:00:47.166 --> 00:00:49.689
Put in v y equals zero and a

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.433
y equals minus g, and it rearranges to

00:00:52.474 --> 00:00:53.855
the height above the launch point:

00:00:54.797 --> 00:00:57.140
H equals u y squared over two g.

00:00:58.203 --> 00:00:59.891
Only the vertical component appears.

00:01:00.475 --> 00:01:02.341
Moving sideways doesn't help the ball climb at

00:01:02.423 --> 00:01:02.522
all.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:03.702
For our ball,

00:01:04.223 --> 00:01:06.468
u y is twenty-five sin fifty,

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.415
about nineteen point one five metres per second.

00:01:10.138 --> 00:01:12.488
Squared, that's about three hundred and sixty-seven.

00:01:13.291 --> 00:01:15.633
Divide by two times nine point eight, which

00:01:15.653 --> 00:01:16.775
is nineteen point six,

00:01:17.315 --> 00:01:19.738
and the maximum height is about eighteen point

00:01:19.778 --> 00:01:21.440
seven metres above the launch point.

00:01:22.049 --> 00:01:23.054
Now the flight time.

00:01:23.598 --> 00:01:25.446
The ball lands when it's back at its

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:28.480
launch level, so its vertical displacement is zero.

00:01:29.261 --> 00:01:31.722
Write s equals u t plus a half

00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:34.104
a t squared for the vertical column, and

00:01:34.165 --> 00:01:34.944
set it to zero:

00:01:35.706 --> 00:01:37.806
u y t minus four point nine t

00:01:37.867 --> 00:01:39.167
squared equals zero.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.555
Take out a factor of t, and there

00:01:41.596 --> 00:01:42.297
are two answers.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.024
t equals zero is the moment of launch,

00:01:45.165 --> 00:01:46.848
when the ball was also at that level,

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.212
so that's not the one we want.

00:01:48.814 --> 00:01:51.322
The other is t equals two u y

00:01:51.564 --> 00:01:52.005
over g.

00:01:52.649 --> 00:01:55.024
That's exactly twice the time to the top.

00:01:55.877 --> 00:01:56.081
Why?

00:01:56.811 --> 00:01:57.532
Gravity takes u

00:01:58.214 --> 00:02:00.097
y away at nine point eight metres per

00:02:00.139 --> 00:02:02.663
second, every second, until it's all gone.

00:02:03.306 --> 00:02:04.631
Then it gives it back at the same

00:02:04.692 --> 00:02:06.579
rate on the way down, so the fall

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.406
takes just as long as the climb.

00:02:08.989 --> 00:02:10.451
For our ball, the time to the top

00:02:10.552 --> 00:02:12.795
is nineteen point one five over nine point

00:02:12.836 --> 00:02:15.860
eight, about one point nine five seconds, so

00:02:15.881 --> 00:02:18.224
the whole flight takes about three point nine

00:02:18.305 --> 00:02:18.805
one seconds.

00:02:19.449 --> 00:02:20.336
So, the landing.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.568
The horizontal component hasn't changed: still sixteen point

00:02:24.689 --> 00:02:25.630
one metres per second.

00:02:26.213 --> 00:02:28.783
The vertical component is back to nineteen point

00:02:28.885 --> 00:02:31.193
one five, but now it points down.

00:02:31.896 --> 00:02:33.557
Those are the same two sizes as at

00:02:33.578 --> 00:02:36.419
launch, so the landing speed is twenty-five metres

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.641
per second again, the same as the launch

00:02:38.682 --> 00:02:38.961
speed.

00:02:39.702 --> 00:02:41.163
Only the direction has changed:

00:02:41.684 --> 00:02:44.405
fifty degrees below the horizontal, instead of fifty

00:02:44.426 --> 00:02:45.226
degrees above.

00:02:46.052 --> 00:02:47.627
And the clock links the columns again.

00:02:48.391 --> 00:02:49.692
The ball is in the air for about

00:02:49.993 --> 00:02:51.594
three point nine one seconds,

00:02:52.116 --> 00:02:54.939
moving sideways at sixteen point zero seven metres

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.302
per second the whole time, so it lands

00:02:57.363 --> 00:02:59.666
about sixty-two point eight metres away.

00:03:00.308 --> 00:03:02.635
These results tell us what controls what.

00:03:03.459 --> 00:03:04.920
Write u y as u

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.683
sin theta, and the height becomes u

00:03:08.405 --> 00:03:11.068
squared sin squared theta over two g,

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.952
while the flight time is two u sin

00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:14.673
theta over g.

00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:18.404
So launch at the same angle, twice as

00:03:18.465 --> 00:03:18.785
fast.

00:03:19.429 --> 00:03:21.322
The flight time just doubles, because it depends

00:03:21.384 --> 00:03:21.483
on u.

00:03:22.149 --> 00:03:24.675
But the height goes up four times, because

00:03:24.716 --> 00:03:26.038
it depends on u squared.

00:03:26.761 --> 00:03:28.985
A faster ball climbs faster, and it also

00:03:29.066 --> 00:03:31.410
keeps climbing for longer, so the two effects

00:03:31.672 --> 00:03:32.152
multiply.

00:03:32.954 --> 00:03:34.718
It's tempting to think everything grows with the

00:03:34.759 --> 00:03:36.844
square of the speed, but the flight time

00:03:37.005 --> 00:03:37.265
doesn't.

00:03:38.098 --> 00:03:38.621
One warning.

00:03:39.225 --> 00:03:41.430
Twice the time to the top, and landing

00:03:41.491 --> 00:03:44.117
at the launch speed, both depend on landing

00:03:44.158 --> 00:03:45.782
at the same level you launched from.

00:03:46.545 --> 00:03:48.869
Launch from a cliff and land lower, and

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.215
the fall lasts longer than the climb, so

00:03:51.417 --> 00:03:52.539
neither shortcut works.

00:03:53.262 --> 00:03:54.371
We'll deal with that case soon.

00:03:55.064 --> 00:03:56.238
Here's how to remember all of this.

00:03:56.983 --> 00:03:59.412
On level ground, the way down mirrors the

00:03:59.452 --> 00:03:59.853
way up.

00:04:00.455 --> 00:04:02.237
The fall takes as long as the climb,

00:04:02.657 --> 00:04:04.719
the ball passes each height at the same

00:04:04.819 --> 00:04:07.261
speed going up and coming down, and it

00:04:07.361 --> 00:04:09.503
lands at the launch speed, at the launch

00:04:09.664 --> 00:04:10.985
angle below the horizontal.

00:04:11.647 --> 00:04:13.932
Just remember, the mirror only works when the

00:04:13.994 --> 00:04:16.038
ball comes back to the level it started

00:04:16.059 --> 00:04:16.219
from.

00:04:19.053 --> 00:04:19.499
Your turn.

00:04:20.188 --> 00:04:23.111
A projectile is launched at fourteen point zero

00:04:23.172 --> 00:04:25.934
metres per second, at forty-five degrees above the

00:04:25.975 --> 00:04:28.617
horizontal, and lands at the same level it

00:04:28.658 --> 00:04:29.278
was launched from.

00:04:30.141 --> 00:04:33.171
Calculate its maximum height and its total time

00:04:33.212 --> 00:04:33.592
of flight.

00:04:34.216 --> 00:04:35.063
Pause here to answer.

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:46.007
First,

00:04:46.589 --> 00:04:49.976
u y is fourteen sin forty-five, about nine

00:04:50.017 --> 00:04:51.298
point nine metres per second.

00:04:52.061 --> 00:04:54.485
The height is u y squared over two

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:54.785
g,

00:04:55.368 --> 00:04:58.152
ninety-eight over nineteen point six, which is five

00:04:58.193 --> 00:04:59.354
point zero zero metres.

00:05:00.137 --> 00:05:02.287
The flight time is two u y over

00:05:02.328 --> 00:05:04.839
g, about two point zero two seconds.

00:05:05.623 --> 00:05:08.070
Using fourteen instead of u y is the

00:05:08.111 --> 00:05:08.793
slip to avoid.

00:05:09.316 --> 00:05:11.342
It gives ten metres and two point eight

00:05:11.383 --> 00:05:11.965
six seconds.

00:05:13.715 --> 00:05:14.143
Last one.

00:05:14.728 --> 00:05:17.370
A projectile is launched at nineteen point six

00:05:17.431 --> 00:05:20.213
metres per second, at thirty degrees above the

00:05:20.254 --> 00:05:22.695
horizontal, and returns to its launch level.

00:05:23.598 --> 00:05:25.702
Calculate the time to reach its highest point

00:05:26.144 --> 00:05:27.526
and its total time of flight,

00:05:28.189 --> 00:05:30.594
and describe its velocity just before it lands.

00:05:31.318 --> 00:05:32.081
Pause here to answer.

00:05:43.788 --> 00:05:47.209
u y is nineteen point six sin thirty,

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.631
which is nine point eight, so the time

00:05:49.652 --> 00:05:51.532
to the top is one point zero zero

00:05:51.593 --> 00:05:54.354
second, and the whole flight takes two point

00:05:54.375 --> 00:05:55.195
zero zero seconds.

00:05:55.916 --> 00:05:58.139
The flight mirrors itself, so it lands at

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:01.004
nineteen point six metres per second, thirty degrees

00:06:01.065 --> 00:06:04.249
below the horizontal, with the horizontal component unchanged

00:06:04.691 --> 00:06:05.972
and the vertical one reversed.

00:06:06.655 --> 00:06:09.043
Giving thirty degrees above is the slip to

00:06:09.104 --> 00:06:09.384
avoid.

00:06:11.175 --> 00:06:13.978
So at equal levels, the vertical component sets

00:06:14.059 --> 00:06:16.342
the height and the flight time, and the

00:06:16.383 --> 00:06:19.267
horizontal component turns that time into a range:

00:06:19.809 --> 00:06:22.031
sixty-two point eight metres for our ball.

00:06:22.854 --> 00:06:25.442
Now launch it at forty degrees instead, at

00:06:25.463 --> 00:06:26.044
the same speed.

00:06:26.607 --> 00:06:28.170
It doesn't go as high, and it comes

00:06:28.211 --> 00:06:31.138
down sooner, yet it lands in exactly the

00:06:31.159 --> 00:06:31.699
same spot.

00:06:32.485 --> 00:06:32.730
Why?

00:06:33.444 --> 00:06:33.887
That's next.

00:06:36.928 --> 00:06:37.750
Here are the key notes.

00:06:38.274 --> 00:06:39.821
Pause the video if you need more time

00:06:39.862 --> 00:06:40.283
to copy them.
